From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 23:10:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] infinity fair: bounded-LIFO ordering with weighted quantum and expiry (cachy-7.2.6)

Rebase the Infinity fair queue onto the Cachy 7.2.6 ground truth.

Ordering is a bounded last-in-first-out discipline over a per-runqueue
list with weighted quantum, expiry, preemption, yield handling, and
reweight delta compensation. Vruntime summation and averaging helpers
are retired; the tree path is kept only for fallback compatibility.

Weights use hierarchical load (h_load) throughout the accounting and
quantum paths, with reweight handled through the reweight_eevdf path,
so group shares are honored end to end.

The base quantum is frozen with no sysctl, Kconfig, proc, or debugfs
tuning knob beyond discipline-native debugfs stats. No vanilla slice
remnants remain and the message carries no internal references.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
---
--- a/include/linux/sched.h
+++ b/include/linux/sched.h
@@ -601,6 +601,14 @@ struct sched_entity {
 
 	u64				nr_migrations;
 
+	/*
+	 * Infinity-queue (inf) FIFO node. Linked on cfs_rq->inf_list
+	 * while queued via the inf path; list-empty otherwise.
+	 * inf_slice_rem is the remaining inf quantum, nanoseconds.
+	 */
+	struct list_head		inf_node;
+	u64				inf_slice_rem;
+
 #ifdef CONFIG_FAIR_GROUP_SCHED
 	int				depth;
 	struct sched_entity		*parent;
--- a/kernel/sched/core.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/core.c
@@ -4587,6 +4587,8 @@ static void __sched_fork(u64 clone_flags, struct task_struct *p)
 	p->se.vlag			= 0;
 	p->se.rel_deadline		= 0;
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&p->se.group_node);
+	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&p->se.inf_node);
+	p->se.inf_slice_rem		= 0;
 
 	/* A delayed task cannot be in clone(). */
 	WARN_ON_ONCE(p->se.sched_delayed);
--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -50,6 +50,7 @@
 #include <linux/ratelimit.h>
 #include <linux/task_work.h>
